introduction:
  bigQuestion: "How do computers learn without being explicitly programmed?"
  overview: "This unit dives into the algorithms of AI. You will distinguishing between <strong>Supervised Learning</strong> (Training with Teacher) and <strong>Unsupervised Learning</strong> (Self-Discovery). You will build <strong>Decision Trees</strong>, map <strong>Clusters</strong>, and understand why 'Overfitting' is the enemy of intelligence."
  journey: "You'll start by teaching computers to classify data using <strong>K-Nearest Neighbours</strong> and <strong>Decision Trees</strong>. Then you'll remove the labels and let the machine find its own patterns using <strong>K-Means Clustering</strong> and <strong>Association Rules</strong>."

concepts:
  - title: "Supervised Learning (Labels)"
    icon: "fa-tags"
    content: |
      <p>The machine learns from examples (Inputs + Correct Answers).</p>
      <ul>
          <li><strong>K-Nearest Neighbours (KNN):</strong> "Tell me who your friends are, and I'll tell you who you are." Classifies based on proximity.</li>
          <li><strong>Decision Trees:</strong> A flowchart of questions (Is it red? Is it round?) to reach a conclusion.</li>
      </ul>

  - title: "Unsupervised Learning (Patterns)"
    icon: "fa-network-wired"
    content: |
      <p>The machine finds structure in chaos (No labels).</p>
      <ul>
          <li><strong>Clustering (K-Means):</strong> Grouping similar items together (e.g., Customer Segments).</li>
          <li><strong>Association Rules:</strong> "People who buy Bread also buy Butter" (Market Basket Analysis).</li>
      </ul>

  - title: "Tuning & Overfitting"
    icon: "fa-sliders"
    content: |
      <p>Finding the Goldilocks Zone.</p>
      <ul>
          <li><strong>Hyperparameters:</strong> Settings we choose (like 'k' in KNN) before training.</li>
          <li><strong>Overfitting:</strong> Memorizing the training data perfectly but failing on new data (Bias/Variance trade-off).</li>
      </ul>

terminology:
  - term: "Supervised Learning"
    definition: "Training a model on a labeled dataset (Input-Output pairs)."
  - term: "Unsupervised Learning"
    definition: "Training a model to find patterns in unlabeled data."
  - term: "K-Nearest Neighbours (KNN)"
    definition: "A classification algorithm that assigns a label based on the majority class of the 'k' closest data points."
  - term: "Decision Tree"
    definition: "A tree-like model of decisions and their possible consequences."
  - term: "Clustering"
    definition: "Grouping a set of objects in such a way that objects in the same group are more similar to each other."
  - term: "Overfitting"
    definition: "When a model learns the noise in the training data rather than the underlying pattern, performing poorly on new data."
  - term: "Hyperparameter"
    definition: "A configuration variable that is external to the model and whose value cannot be estimated from data (e.g., 'k')."
  - term: "Entropy"
    definition: "A measure of impurity or disorder used in Decision Trees to decide where to split."

misconceptions:
  - mistake: "Bigger 'k' is Always Better"
    correction: "No! If 'k' is too big, you lose detail (Underfitting). If 'k' is too small, you capture noise (Overfitting)."
  - mistake: "Clustering = Classification"
    correction: "Classification knows the answers (Cats vs Dogs). Clustering just says 'These things look similar' (Group A vs Group B)."
  - mistake: "Correlation = Causality"
    correction: "Just because 'Bread' and 'Butter' are bought together (Association) doesn't mean Bread CAUSES Butter purchases."

